WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.445 --> 00:00:04.468
Unit thirteen. Avoiding Scams for Kids!

2
00:00:05.379 --> 00:00:10.145
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.195 --> 00:00:13.276
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.326 --> 00:00:17.487
Today we learn about Avoiding Scams for Kids. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:22.589
Scam. Say it with me. Scam!

6
00:00:26.094 --> 00:00:29.594
Trick. Say it with me. Trick!

7
00:00:33.094 --> 00:00:38.094
Too good to be true. Say it with me. Too good to be true!

8
00:00:41.628 --> 00:00:46.061
Suspicious. Say it with me. Suspicious!

9
00:00:49.573 --> 00:00:53.926
Never click. Say it with me. Never click!

10
00:00:57.425 --> 00:01:01.755
Tell an adult. Say it with me. Tell an adult!

11
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.976
Warning. Say it with me. Warning!

12
00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:16.489
Careful. Say it with me. Careful!

13
00:01:19.992 --> 00:01:30.385
A scam tries to trick me, often with an offer that seems too good to be true. I stay suspicious, never click, and tell an adult about a warning sign.

14
00:01:30.435 --> 00:01:34.173
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:40.758
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.808 --> 00:01:42.644
Too good to be true!

17
00:01:43.514 --> 00:01:48.949
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.999 --> 00:01:50.149
Warning!

19
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:59.611
Did you know? A common rule is: if an online offer seems too good to be true, it usually is!

20
00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:02.151
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:02.851 --> 00:02:12.982
Think and answer. What is a warning sign that something online might be a scam?

22
00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.289
Great answer!

23
00:02:15.288 --> 00:02:21.303
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:21.353 --> 00:02:24.508
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

